%N A399855 a(n) is the least k > 1 such that the factorial base expansion of n appears as a substring in that of k*n.
%C A399855 The sequence is well defined (see A399856).
%H A399855 Rémy Sigrist, <a href="/A399855/b399855.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..5040</a>
%H A399855 Rémy Sigrist, <a href="/A399855/a399855.txt">C program</a>
%H A399855 <a href="/index/Fa#facbase">Index entries for sequences related to factorial base representation</a>
%F A399855 a(k!) = k + 1 for any k > 0.
%e A399855 The first terms, alongside their factorial base expansion, are:
%e A399855   n   a(n)  fact(n)  fact(a(n)*n)
